Mon Oct 26 08:06:36 UTC 2026 - Dirk Müller <dmueller@suse.com>

- update to 1.37:
  * Clean up in-place output after write errors
  * Reject invalid patch document containers
  * Use UTF-8 for JSON command-line file I/O
  * Handle source pointer objects in move location helpers
- update to 1.36:
  * Honor optimization=False when generating patches
  * Preserve the original file when in-place CLI replacement
    fails
- update to 1.35:
  * Refactor JsonPatch class and improve documentation
  * Add pytest configuration for non-standard test file naming
  * Document JSON Pointer escaping for special characters
  * Improve list diffing to avoid unnecessary item replacements
  * Use correct SPDX-Identifer
  * Improve coverage reporting by combining test runs
  * ci: run tests on every PR and pushes to master
  * Add support for Python 3.13 and 3.14
  * Improve list diffing with sequence alignment to avoid
    cascading changes
  * Handle self-containing values in make_patch and add #180
    regression tests
  * Only reject '-' in replace when it refers to an array
  * Reject moving any location into its own children, fixes #214
  * Compare values in 'test' by JSON equality
  * Hash patch operations by their 'op' and 'path'
  * Require jsonpointer>=3.2
  * Raise documented exceptions for malformed patches and "from":
    "/-"
  * Support whole document operations on scalar documents
  * Housekeeping: stale links, packaging cleanup, CI action
    versions
  * Find moves in make_patch without rewriting all later
    operations
  * Close test coverage gaps
  * Remove unreachable code from make_patch and the jsonpointer <
    3.2 shim
  * Test the index helpers of PatchOperation and MoveOperation
  * Upload coverage to Coveralls again
  * Close the original input before in-place replacement
  * Install the command line programs as console_scripts
- update to 1.34:
  * Update documentation to include a link to the GitHub repo and
    installation instructions
  * Support only currently supported Python versions (by @hf-
    kklein in #155, #156, @CyrilRoelandteNovance in #162,
    @stefankoegl in #193)
  * fix: remove unused exception variables (F841)
  * Avoid usage of unittest.makeSuite, removed from Python 3.13
  * Handle the whole-document pointer in the sequence branch
  * Fix copying from the whole-document pointer
  * Add property-based tests using Hypothesis
  * DiffBuilder: fix reindexing of operations involving nested
    paths
  * fix: use deterministic comparison ordering
  * Fix `_compare_lists` treating `1` and `True` as equal in JSON
    diff by @stefankoegl with @Copilot in
    https://github.com/stefankoegl/python-json-patch/pull/181
  * Update property test counterexamples for fixes from #175 and
    #181
  * Prevent RFC 6901 pointer indexing into strings
  * DiffBuilder: fix operation reindexing bug
  * Fix patch operations to not modify patch object during apply
  * Refactor DiffBuilder to use tuple paths and simplify
    operation handling
  * Fix ReadTheDocs configuration and documentation build
  * Clarify patch application semantics and fix documentation
  * Add PyPI publishing workflow and update release process

